Level 10 → Level 11

Concept
This one hands you the password encoded in Base64 instead of plain 
text. Base64 isn't encryption — it's just a way of representing data 
using a fixed set of readable characters, commonly used to safely 
transmit binary-ish data as text. The level is testing whether you 
know how to decode it back to its original form.

Commands used
cat data.txt
echo "<base64 string from data.txt>" | base64 -d

Why it works
cat data.txt just revealed the encoded string. Piping that string into 
base64 -d reverses the encoding — the -d flag tells the base64 command 
to decode rather than encode — converting it back into the original 
readable password.
